Michael remembers exactly what went  through his head the day he was  diagnosed with HIV it was in January  last year he knew his life had changed  forever you know not only is it my first  thought was will I still be able to find  work oh no I'm positive I had this idea  of jumping off a bridge I was thinking  oh my god I need to die oh my god I need  to die  Michael is 21 and one of some 35,000  people known to live with HIV in the  Philippines he fears being stigmatized  so he asked us not to show his face as a  teenager he sold sex to other men often  without using a condom knowledge about  HIV and how the virus is transmitted is  still patchy among many Filipinos the  ignorance leads not only to higher  infection rates but also feeds fear and  rejection after years of playing down  how severely hiv/aids is impacting young  men like Michael the government now  seems to be changing course  critics have already forced officials to  scrap the idea of making condoms  available at schools they're afraid it  would encourage children to become  promiscuous conservatives say sex  education doesn't belong in the  classroom the first teachers of the  children are their parents for heaven's  sake the parents are not only supposed  to give them food board and lodging but  also to teach them value system  behavioral patterns etc etc to be good  members of society sexual education it  belongs to the parish themselves it's  not an approach Michael things can work  neither parents nor teenagers feel  comfortable talking about sex he himself  has become a peer educator he wants to  spare other young people his fatal agama  goombah say everything starts with  knowing once people have adequate  knowledge  right information about hiv/aids teen  pregnancy condoms and other things  you'll be armed your knowledge will be  your shield and your sword that way you  can protect yourself and at the same  time protect other young people  especially those who are close to you  John Michael knows he's facing an uphill  battle but for him every HIV case he can  prevent by sharing what he's had to  learn the hard way is a victory
 

